<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abam</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Abam are an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/igbo-people">Igbo</a> clan of modern Abia State in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>. Renowned as warriors, they served the Aro Confederacy as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a> in the 18th and 19th centuries, raiding communities that defied Aro authority and helping to supply captives for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">slave trade</a>. Their martial traditions survive in dances and ceremonies.</p></div>
